  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "DotCov 3.0.1 fixes CRAP passes that 3.0.0 could not prove; line and branch gates are unchanged.\nCRAP: an unmeasured metrics method, an ambiguous overload match or a complexity below 1 now gives NODATA (exit 3); async overloads keep their own body, so diluted scores rise; state-machine-only async overloads match their metrics rows; function-pointer parameters no longer abort crap; declarations without a body need no coverage; --source-root also roots relative metrics paths; Visual Basic metrics displays match.\nExclusions: excluded methods count as measured without a score and never hide a kept sibling; merged reports no longer list a re-added file as excluded.\nDotCov.Fallout requires System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs/Xml 10.0.13.\nFull notes: https://github.com/ANcpLua/dotcov/blob/main/docs/releases/3.0.1.md",
